390	     * gives the claim the sheet's next number; a voided claim keeps it (the number is never given again).
391	     * Opening records who opened it; that user cannot settle it (403).
392	     * Settling fixes the claim's due at its person's grade's rate in force on the claim's date, raised to
393	     * the sheet's floor, with its late charge added if it is overdue; later floor and late percent changes
394	     * leave it as fixed. Every rounding is half up for a claim dated before the sheet's policy date and
395	     * half to even otherwise; later policy date changes leave it as fixed too. A correction's due is its amount times that rate, rounded the same way, with no
396	     * floor and no late charge. A clerk
397	     * can settle a claim only when that due is at or below the sheet's clerk limit, if it has one (403);
398	     * a claim with no due (no rate) is then refused too, as it cannot be shown to be within the limit.
